KZ3 patch 2064 (RSX pass 63): NV40 half/full register aliasing in the fragment decompiler (LD_FP_ALIAS=0 = old).
rsx_fp_decompiler.c: the half and full temp files are one register file: h[2k] is the low 64 bits of r[k] (h.x/h.y
= the low/high halves of r[k].x, h.z/h.w those of r[k].y), h[2k+1] the high 64 bits. KZ3's G-buffer programs write
the view normal to h0.xy and read r0.x (the two halves as one word) for UPB into the bytes of the normals target
0x16C0000; the decompiler kept r[] and h[] apart, so r0.x read 0 and every light saw the normal (0,0,1): flat,
overbright lit surfaces. fp_alias_scan pre-scans the program for registers read through the other view (plus the
colour exports of the selected file); after each write, fp_alias_mirror refreshes exactly those aliased
components (asfloat(f32tof16 pack) of the halves, or f16tof32 of the word's halves). Programs that never read
across the views are byte-identical. A text scan of the 145 K2 programs dumped in pass 63 flags up to 99 that read across (an upper bound). Host test
tools/smoke/test_fp_alias.sh. As RPCS3's fragment decompiler (register gather/split), read for reference.
Upstream candidate (general NV40 semantics).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.15.0 (SPU pass 81): context only, upstream gamma-unit scan inserted at the same spot, pack flag from upstream.

